From: logos-node-android
Subject: [PATCH 0001] Fast replay of the node's own stored blocks at startup

Against logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain tag 0.3.4. Applied with
`git apply -p1` by native/apply-patches.sh. See native/patches/README.md.

At startup the chain service replays every stored block after the LIB, and
each one is verified again in full (leader proof, deferred transaction proofs).
With this patch, blocks this same build already verified replay without those
two proof checks. A marker file next to the database records the build and the
tip and LIB of the chain the running node holds and verified; it is rewritten
whenever the node records its recovery state. At the next start, only the
marker's tip and its ancestors replay fast, and only if the marker is from this
build and the stored LIB is the marker's LIB. Every other block (and every
block when LOGOS_REPLAY_VERIFY=full) is verified in full, exactly as upstream.

Blocks from the network are verified exactly as before. No change to consensus
rules, wire formats, the database format, the config file or the HTTP API.

